cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "The Harness Effect: measuring how much of LLM capability is the scaffold"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Esposito Brescia"
    given-names: "Alessandro"
    affiliation: "Rebis Labs"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Rebis-Labs/the-harness-effect"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-07-21
keywords:
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - agent harness
  - tool use
  - benchmarks
  - local llm
abstract: >-
  Observed capability = model x harness. A minimal, dependency-free lab that
  holds the harness constant to measure the model, then holds the model
  constant to measure the harness. On a frozen 9-task tool-use benchmark, a
  local 14B Q4 model went from 33% to 100% through harness changes alone.
